From 9eb188d230584db861af852da9bc61c7cdd7ea9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:44:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): no-progress budget stops re-spawning cards whose
 runs change nothing [daveey]

t_e3e216d4 spent 141 runs (10-23..11-10) on clock wakes that re-read an
unchanged graph, commented and parked again; t_01a1a27deb10165f 599 on a
probe that kept breaking. No guard saw it: the crash breaker counts failures,
max_continuations counts back-to-back `continued` only, card waits are exempt
from the 3x re-park escalation.

kanban_no_progress (hooked in lane_admission_refused, before any claim) counts
trailing waiting runs since the last progress marker (status hand-off, link,
attachment, edit, move, contract, condition_met, human comment, linked-card
completion/review/edit; agent comments and bare unblocks are not progress,
run losses neutral, declared clock windows exempt, clock polls 1/4). At
kanban.no_progress_runs (default 5, 0 off), re-decided under the write lock
and never under a live claim, it re-parks behind this episode's own wake
condition (24 h fallback) or files one idempotent owner card the card waits
on; a looping owner card goes to triage. No continuation_exhausted /
goal_unachievable is written, so no recovery loop.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_no_progress.py 23 pass; 5 fail with the
admission hook removed; 21 anchor mutants killed; 92 kanban dispatch/guard/
continuation files 1343 pass. Replay over every hub board (read-only, at each
run's start): 41 cards held, 976 runs not spawned, 32 park / 14 escalate
episodes; t_e3e216d4 101/142 caught. Card t_01a1c7d033912ae9.
